From ad92e89fa464f282e23d8ca00f0123da9d6390b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:01:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(sim): play the stock up to the first operation with
 no toolpath

The traced stock playback refused the whole setup when one operation
had no toolpath. It now plays the program in posting order up to the
first operation with no toolpath and stops there; it never skips that
operation to cut the ones after it. A separate line under the transport
bar names the operation in plain English, so the status line keeps the
generation notes without the error mark. The post and the Deviate
verdict keep program_ops / plan_program and still refuse by name.

Fixes #2280

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
